    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d540">

                <pb facs="0969" n="865" xml:id="pg865"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW
                    1939/32572: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-01-06">January 6, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>43, January 6, 4 p.m. Personal and secret for the President and the Secretary
                    from Harriman:</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Molotov<anchor n="1" xml:id="d540-f1"/>
                    continued that Marshal Stalin at Tehran
                    had outlined the terms which the Soviet Government were prepared to accord
                    Finland and, as he recalled it, the President and Mr. Churchill had expressed no objection to these terms.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d540-f2"/></p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Harriman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d540-f1" n="1" xml:id="d540-f1-content">
                <p>In the course of a conversation with Harriman on December 31, 1943.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d540-f2" n="2" xml:id="d540-f2-content">
